BlackHole (as "PlugInput.driver")
---------------------------------

The audio driver installed at /Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/HAL/PlugInput.driver is a MODIFIED
build of BlackHole by Existential Audio Inc.

    Upstream:  https://github.com/ExistentialAudio/BlackHole
    Version:   v0.6.1
    Copyright: Existential Audio Inc.
    License:   GNU General Public License v3.0

THIS IS NOT THE OFFICIAL BLACKHOLE BINARY, AND IT IS NOT SUPPORTED BY EXISTENTIAL AUDIO.
Please report any problem with PlugInput to PlugInput's own issue tracker, not to them.

What was modified
-----------------

Nothing in the source. The driver is built from an unmodified v0.6.1 checkout with three
compile-time constants overridden, so that the device appears under its own name and does not
collide with an existing BlackHole installation:

    kDriver_Name     = "PlugInput"
    kDevice_Name     = "PlugInput"
    kPlugIn_BundleID = "com.pluginput.driver"

Corresponding source (GPLv3 section 6)
--------------------------------------

The corresponding source is BlackHole v0.6.1 as published at the URL above, together with
make-driver.sh in this repository, which pins that exact tag and records every build flag
applied to it. Both are publicly available, which satisfies the obligation to accompany the
binary with its source.

The full GPL-3.0 text also ships inside the installed driver bundle, at
/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/HAL/PlugInput.driver/Contents/Resources/LICENSE.

Relationship to the app
-----------------------

PlugInput.app links no BlackHole code. It communicates with the driver through CoreAudio's
public interfaces, as any audio application does with any audio device. Shipping both in one
installer is mere aggregation under GPLv3 section 5, so the app's own MIT license is unaffected.
